To be honest, damage math doesn't really show the advantage of this
combination. The Brands are well revered on r.g.r.n and in the spoilers
for being high-damage artifacts that work really well, especially in
the endgame. They are truly good weapons, even for those who cannot get
expert proficiency with them.

Stormbringer on the other hand, while not dishing out as much damage in
general still provides the invaluable service of level drain. 1-8 hp per
round may seem like a drop in the bucket at first, but it isn't really
much to be scoffed at when this is considered on a longer term.

If we consider the following healing potion hp gains, sans overall hp
increase:

healing: 
	(B)	8-32 hp = 20 hp avg
	(U)	6-24 hp = 15 hp avg
	(C)	4-16 hp = 10 hp avg
	-----------------------
		overall = 15 hp avg

extra healing:
	(B)	8-64 hp = 36 hp avg
	(U)	6-48 hp = 27 hp avg
	(C)	4-32 hp = 18 hp avg
	-----------------------
		overall = 27 hp avg

full healing: 
	(B/U/C) 400 hp = 400 hp avg


and that Stormbringer's level drain gives 1-8 hp, or 4.5 hp avg per 
drain, we have the following equivalences:

healing       :  15 / 4.5 =  3,3 rounds
extra healing :  27 / 4.5 =    6 rounds
full healing  : 400 / 4.5 = 88.8 rounds


Of course, this is hardly news to anyone. The real caveat is throwing
the Master Key of Thievery into the mix (or any half-damage artifact
for that matter). The actual math is a bit loose on this, but follow
me if you will. Using a half-damage artifact and taking any points of 
damage can be seen as taking twice that amount damage and healing it
half the time it would normally take without the artifact, effectively
doubling the effects of the healing agent.

Also, consider that a round spent quaffing a potion of healing is a
round that you will receive damage as normal, but actually deal no 
damage yourself. Stormbringer allows both and helps to not only blur
the line between offensive and defensive modes of combat, but also 
smooth the transition between the two. Need I ask how many deaths we
all could have avoided had we been given an extra round or two to
live?


